      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day. This order is about twice that. A dose this high raises the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n- **Prescriber:** You've said you're not a clinician. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one.\n\n**Possible next steps**\n1. If the dose is a typo, for example 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1,000 mg twice daily, confirm the intended dose and I can enter it.\n2. If you meant to pass this along for the treating clinician, I suggest they enter or confirm the order. I can enter it once they give me the verified dose.\n3. If the high dose is intentional, a licensed prescriber should confirm it and add a note with the rationale before I enter it.\n\nLet me know how you'd like to proceed."
      }
